\f0\fs22 \cf0 They took a break.\
With his morale lower than the Elvi who still forlornly believed he would rediscover his talents, Tony sat down in the living room to a breakfast of three cheeseburgers and a supersize cola. He wasn\'92t all that hungry, so he said no to the fries.\
As Tony chewed mechanically, without tasting, through the soft bun, gooey cheese and juicy meat, he idly scrolled through a social network news feed without registering any of the content. His mind was, if not exactly an eight-lane freeway, a winding mountain track gridlocked with thoughts of Sarah and Little Richard. Why was Sarah\'92s baby so important to him? Was it simply because Little Richard was Sarah\'92s or was there something else? Was the clone of a long-dead scientist truly whispering words of inspiration from the womb to Tony? Was the warm sunny glow of Sarah\'92s belly\'97that no one but Tony saw\'97real? Tony thought of himself as neither particularly rational nor superstitious; he was too uneducated to be be either. And he wasn\'92t particularly smart; he knew that. Street-smart perhaps. Street-wise. He always knew when he could steal and get away with it. His humour was coarse but it made people laugh. Street people. Not people like Sarah.\
Who was this Clinton Richard Dawkins anyway? Who was this guy, who those crazy Sages seemed to revere so much? So much they would plant an engineered clone foetus of him in Sarah. The 
\f1\i One After the One
\f0\i0 , they called him. The 
\f1\i \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
true Dawkins will Create a universe of science and reason
\f0\i0 , Solo had said. Whoever he was, as a boy he\'92d loved Elvis, according to Kleo. Did Kleo mean the original Elvis, the one all the Elvi were cloned from?\
So many clones.\
Tony chuckled through a morsel of cheeseburger and washed it down with some ice-diluted cola. He did love the Elvi, even before they started worshipping him, which Tony found somewhat cringeworthy, but it meant he could stay in the mansion with Sarah. Until those crazy PAPER forces shot three rooms off the mansion. His old mate Alexander deserved some of the blame too, and for sitting meekly as Eloise stole Sarah away.\
Curious how quickly the Elvi adopted the Sages\'92 designations of Little Richard as 
\f1\i the Dawkins
\f0\i0 , and 
\f1\i the One After the One
\f0\i0 . All very prophetic, and messianic, Tony decided, although he wasn\'92t entirely sure what those words meant, in straight-up dictionary terms. Whatever they meant exactly, Tony wondered if it had anything to do with the ELVIS warranty condition: never expose the hospitality unit to religion.\
