<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi erupted with a cheering roar, mobbed Tony, and lifted him high above their heads. In a seething mass, they surged towards the living room door, perhaps to carry him exultantly out to the street. Unfortunately, they slammed him head-first into the beam above the door. He fell to the floor, apparently dead.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Silently and reverently, a chosen few carried Tony to his room and laid him gently on his unmade bed. Some kissed his forehead. Others hunkered down to keep vigil over his body.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At about four in the morning a cry went up around the studio. 
\f1\i He is risen! He is risen!
\f0\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>That morning, Tony ate a large plate of fries, along with three cheeseburgers and supersize cola.
